Z||000000||Gonzo_442||11-19-2001||11:13 AM||||Just a quick note, the time has come to replace the stock exhaust on my 87GT. i've been looking around and i was wondering if anyone has had any experience with the ocelot setup from the fiero store. Good, bad, indifferent? Sound nice? <P>A local shop took a look at the sprint manifolds the fiero store offers, and he claims he can match the price, including the heat coating. I was wondering if these were any better then just porting the stock ones.<P>Interested in any thoughts. Thanks.<P>--<BR>G||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||11-19-2001||11:44 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Gonzo_442:<BR><B>Just a quick note, the time has come to replace the stock exhaust on my 87GT. i've been looking around and i was wondering if anyone has had any experience with the ocelot setup from the fiero store. Good, bad, indifferent? Sound nice? <P>A local shop took a look at the sprint manifolds the fiero store offers, and he claims he can match the price, including the heat coating. I was wondering if these were any better then just porting the stock ones.<P>Interested in any thoughts. Thanks.<P>--<BR>G</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The Ocelot is better than stock but if you want a good stainless exhaust, get a Borla System. (Ocelot isn't stainless, it's aluminized, still corrodes) Twin Lakes is setting up to sell them.  The Sprint headers are better than ported stock by a very slight bit performance wise and alot better durability. They won't crack like the stock ones. Even after fixing an original one they can still crack. Chris West also makes "shorty" headers.<P><P>------------------<BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">          <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Happiness isn't around the corner...<BR>Happiness IS the corner.</I></B></FONT>||||reg||1
